A||N||21||cscougar||K & N Air filter||||1||
Z||000000||cscougar||10-30-2000||10:05 PM||||Is the K & N Air Filter worth the $30.00 investment for a 2.8 V-6?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Ed||10-30-2000||10:09 PM||||Yes.  I've been happy with mine.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||10-30-2000||10:17 PM||||All the way!!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/singnit3_1.gif">   <BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000003||pHoOl||10-30-2000||10:21 PM||||how much of a performance difference does it really make?<BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||SibERThuG||10-30-2000||10:56 PM||||I noticed throttle response right away of the start and at a higher speeds. I am so happy with mine. Best $30 spent. Add a side scoop and pull the "air dam" out, and whoa! Watch out! Faster car. More powerful car. Happier owner!<P>------------------<BR>Robbie<BR>88' Formula||||reg||10
Z||000005||mrfiero||10-30-2000||11:18 PM||||I like the K&N for a different reason.  While a little better airflow is good, I like it because Denver is a pretty dusty town.  I could go through 2 or 3 paper filters in a years time.  At $10 or so each, the $30 initial cost for the K&N is nothing.  Add a few more $$ for a recharge kit and within 2 years it pays for itself.<P>I have used the same K&N in 6 different Fieros!  Everytime I sell one I take it out and reinstall in the "new" one.<P>Bottom line.....buy one!!||||reg||1
Z||000006||DaRkLoRD||10-31-2000||12:27 AM||||I've heard a lot of pros and cons regarding the performance aspect of a K&N filter on the Fiero.. (the cons being that it doesn't improve performance.. hehe)<P>It does improve airflow, but since the Fiero intake is already very efficient, there might not be a major improvement with a stock engine. On other cars, which come with a less efficient intake setup, there might be up to a 20HP increase. The filter isn't making the engine perform better, it's simply allowing it to perform at closer to it's peak power. I'm getting a K&N filter in a custom ram air tube for my GT. With the way I've designed the intake pipe and filter shroud, I'm expecting some performance gains. Not a lot, but there should be some increase.<P>However the best advantage to a K&N filter with a stock engine is the fact that it can be re-used many times over, which saves money.<P>So, in general.. I'd have to agree that installing a K&N filter is a good modification to do. Make sure it's piped down to the intake grate though, otherwise you'll be sucking in hot air from the engine bay!<P>------------------<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>   <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 10-31-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000007||1FST2M6||10-31-2000||09:08 AM||||yeah i know... you saw it comming... <P>Heres is dyno proof what the K&N does on a 24,000 engine 86 V6 GT 4spd. Measured on a Dynojet model 248c. yes it's worth the money cause you'll NEVER have to replace it again! <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BlackGTdyno_3.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>Shhh.. Top Secret! <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstcheeto_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||stimpy||10-31-2000||01:13 PM||||I also noticed quicker throttle response. But the main benefit is it's the last one you'll ever have to buy.||||reg||1
Z||000009||colts60||11-02-2000||06:35 PM||||is there a major benefit to putting one on a <BR>4cyl<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000010||KnightRyder31||11-02-2000||08:49 PM||||I have a four cyl. I did infact notice a reasonable diff. I would back it 100%!! There is more response, and some more HP. I dont care what anyone says, it DOES increase HP, and it is some-what noticable. ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Black88GT||11-02-2000||10:26 PM||||I am not flaming anyone, but I don't know how you guys could notice a better throttle response by adding an air filter.  The dyno shows a 2hp increase which is not noticeable by ass-o-meter recordings.  I think it is definitely a great air filter for the reasons Mike (mrfiero) gave, lasts forever and it pays for itself in a few years.  Performance wise, I don't think it changes a thing except maybe 1 or 2 Hp over a dirty air filter.<P>IMHO of course<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
Z||000012||ka4nkf||11-03-2000||10:48 PM||||the best way to test this K&N filter Is as follows. (BTW  most of you notice a difference bacause the filter you took out was probably dirty, even a new paper filter would have made a difference), also I dont recall seeing a K&N filter on any winston cup race car. now If you really want to test It, go some place and mark off a quarter of a mile, then remove you filter completly and give It a run, maybe two. then put the K&N filter In and give It another run or two. I bet you dont see any difference.||||reg||1
Z||000013||JohnnyK||11-04-2000||01:50 AM||||I agree totally with Black88GT.. You will not notice any HP increase.. However, if you really need a new air filter, and you have $ to spend.. Do it up.. It's reusable..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000014||WKDFIRO||11-04-2000||02:40 AM||||Since when do Winston Cup engines need to worry about having the engine intact in 20,000 miles or 100,000 miles? Dragsters don't have an air filter either but that doesn't mean a lot! Both engines are rebuilt and torn down so much that it doesn't matter.<P>Air filters are for the long haul going down the highway and making sure that the road grime and dirt doesnt' choke off the engine in 50,000 miles...it would be a great thing to prove the flow of a K&N filter if you can't feel the difference with or without it!<P> The real difference is if you run the engine constantly without a filter and compare it to one with. Hate to think what kind of filth would be forming around the valves after a year!||||reg||1
Z||000015||ka4nkf||11-04-2000||05:17 AM||||Let me say one thing, If you put In a new Fram filter and run then run the quarter mile. then put in a new K&N filter and run the quaretr mile you will see no difference. (Btw the way winstom cup cars use one paper filter and sometimes two) Dont get me wrong but K&N filter are great filters, well made and top quality. but I just dont see paying $30.00 plus for a air cleaner Its like paying $5.00 Or more for a splitfire pulg when It wont do as good as a AC.||||reg||1
Z||000016||88formula||11-04-2000||10:45 AM||||I think you people forgot that one of the reasons the K+N filter works to increase airflow is because it straightens out the air so there is less turbulence, which increases flow. That is why an engine can flow more air with the filter installed than it can without any filter at all.||||reg||1
Z||000017||ThatRickGuy||11-04-2000||10:52 AM||||I wish I still had the link for the site, I got it off the classical pontiac board, but one of the racers over there tested the heck out of the differences in air filters. basically, between 1/4 tests, dynos, and airflow testing, he came up with the following ranking:<P>3) Stock Filter<BR>2) No Filter<BR>1) K&N<P>I don't remeber the exact numbers, and the difference wasn't huge, but on the 1/4 mile, 2 hp can make a difference. The reason behind the K&N doing better then the no filter was because it helps air flow, unlike the lack of filter which allows air to tumble. All in all, monitarily a good investment, and if you get a few hp for it, all the better.||||reg||1
Z||000018||SeanyD||11-04-2000||11:29 AM||||On the cars I race I can say that yes K&N's make a huge difference. we use con filters on our carbs and run on a dirt track...problem with the cotton gauze ones was even after being sprayed with filter oil before and washed after every use, they just didn't seem to breath as well as the K&N ones....the K-n filters just held more surface area over the other and kept more dirt out||||reg||1
Z||000019||KnightRyder31||11-04-2000||03:48 PM||||K&N is the better filter, hands down. I actually ran my car without a filter on the way to pick up my new K&N, It was about 6 miles. I thought that when I put the K&N in, it would slow my car down for sure, I didnt understand how 1 filter could be better then no filter(Performence wise) . Well folks, I was wrong. It was better then running it without a filter! <BR>Anyways, I CAN tell the diff. And I think that the K&N gave me about 5-10HP. <P>I think Formula said it best, K&N straightens your air flow, thus increasing airflow, hence increases HP.<P>[This message has been edited by KnightRyder31 (edited 11-04-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by KnightRyder31 (edited 11-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||gixxer||11-04-2000||04:26 PM||||No noticable difference on my V6.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000021||StuGood||11-04-2000||05:17 PM||||Thought about trying a K&N filter a few years ago, when I wasn't sure how long they'd be making air filters for the Fiero V6.  But after I saw the price of the K&N, I decided paper filters can't be all bad  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  And of course, there're so many 2.8's and 3.1's out there which use the same filter, I doubt they'll quit making the paper filters anytime soon.  <P>The beauty of a mod like this, is that it's so reversible!  No like? - change back! It's a whole lot faster and easier to change an air filter than plugs!  So someday, I'll probably get the extra-long prybar out, extract money from the time capsule (my wallet), and give K&N a try.   <P>BTW, if I can't <B>tell</B> any difference, I don't consider it a successful mod.   So you won't see me instrumenting my car just to see if it did anything. Does K&N give your money back if you don't like it?<P>One concern: You can't tell how good a cleaning job the filter is doing.  Not until it's too late. <P>One thing ||||reg||1
